infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title The consistency split: search vs reserve
  desc Two paths, opposite consistency needs — that's the whole architecture
  compares
    - label Availability search
      children
        - label ~10,000 searches/sec
          desc The dominant load (~100x of bookings)
        - label Eventually consistent
          desc Served from caches and read replicas
        - label Advisory and slightly stale
          desc The number you see is an estimate, not a guarantee
        - label Read-optimized
          desc Denormalized for fast date-range queries
    - label Reservation
      children
        - label ~100-1,000 bookings/sec
          desc Tiny vs search, but correctness-critical
        - label Strongly consistent
          desc Single-shard by hotel, one local ACID transaction
        - label Atomic check-and-decrement
          desc All-or-nothing across every night in the range
        - label The only real guarantee
          desc Prevents the double-booking entirely
theme
  palette #0ea5e9 #f43f5e
